The fonts that ship with bateri: one directory per family, unmodified copies
of the upstream files, each with its license text and a README that names the
source, the version and the sha256 of what it holds. `make bundle` copies this
tree to `Contents/Resources/fonts` and checks it against `SHA256SUMS` (`make
fonts-sums` writes the list again after a deliberate change).

At launch the fonts are registered for the bateri process only, so they appear
in bateri's Font list and nowhere else on the Mac. A family the user installed
under the same name is left alone: their copy opens, not this one.

| directory | Font list name | files |
|---|---|---|
| JetBrainsMono | JetBrains Mono | variable, roman and italic |
| FiraCode | Fira Code | variable, roman (no italic design) |
| CascadiaCode | Cascadia Code | variable, roman and italic |
| MonaspaceNeon | Monaspace Neon | static, four faces |
| GeistMono | Geist Mono | variable, roman and italic |
| MapleMono | Maple Mono | variable, roman and italic |
| IBMPlexMono | IBM Plex Mono | static, four faces |
| ObelMono | Obel Mono | variable, roman and italic |
| SymbolsNerdFontMono | (not listed) | one file: the symbols drawn where the selected font has none |

The font files add up to 9,287,652 bytes (9.3 MB) in the package.

Obel Mono and JetBrains Mono also serve the tests (`coretext::fixture`).
